{% block title %}GFI-CO GROUP | Privacy Policy{% endblock %}
{% block description %}Privacy Policy and information about the processing of personal data by GFI-CO GROUP.{% endblock %}
{% block bread_subtitle %}Data protection{% endblock %}
{% block bread_title %}Privacy Policy{% endblock %}
{% block bread_items %}<li class="active">Privacy Policy</li>{% endblock %}
{% block draft_notice %}<p><strong>Last updated: date to be completed.</strong> GFI-CO must confirm operational information about its providers, data retention and any international transfers before publication.</p>{% endblock %}

{% block document_content %}
    <h2>1. Purpose</h2>
    <p>This policy explains how GFI-CO SARL may collect, use, retain and protect personal data when you visit <a href="https://www.gfi-co.net/">www.gfi-co.net</a> or contact the company. It is intended to operate within the framework of applicable law in Côte d’Ivoire, including Law No. 2013-450 of 19 June 2013 on the protection of personal data.</p>

    <h2>2. Data controller</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Controller: GFI-CO SARL</li>
        <li>Address: [full official address to be confirmed]</li>
        <li>Email: <a href="mailto:contact@gfi-co.net">contact@gfi-co.net</a></li>
        <li>Telephone: [official number to be confirmed]</li>
        <li>Personal data contact, if applicable: [name and contact details to be completed]</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Data that may be collected</h2>
    <h3>3.1. Forms</h3>
    <p>Depending on the form and the fields actually shown, data may include your name, email address, telephone number, enquiry subject and message, and information about your project. The fields displayed on each form determine what is requested. Please provide only information relevant to your enquiry.</p>
    <h3>3.2. Technical data</h3>
    <p>Depending on the actual configuration, the server or technical components may record an IP address, connection date and time, pages viewed, browser and operating system, and technical information needed to operate and secure the website. The configuration and log retention periods must be verified.</p>
    <h3>3.3. WhatsApp and maps</h3>
    <p>The website provides WhatsApp contact options and embeds an OpenStreetMap map. Opening these services may send technical information to the relevant provider. Messages sent through WhatsApp are also subject to that service’s terms and privacy policy. The details depend on the actual configuration and communications.</p>

    <h2>4. Purposes</h2>
    <p>Data may be used to respond to contact requests, review enquiries or quotation requests and real estate projects, follow up on communications, provide requested information about GFI-CO SARL’s services, operate, maintain and secure the website, prevent abuse and meet applicable legal obligations. Data should not be reused for incompatible purposes.</p>
    <p>The website does not currently offer newsletter registration, so form data should not automatically subscribe anyone to a newsletter. Any later marketing use must be appropriately disclosed and, where required, based on consent.</p>

    <h2>5. Legal basis</h2>
    <p>The legal basis must be identified for each processing activity according to its purpose and applicable rules. Depending on the case, this may be consent where required, pre-contractual steps requested by the individual, a legal obligation, or another applicable and justified basis. Sending an enquiry does not authorise every later use of the data.</p>

    <h2>6. Required and optional fields</h2>
    <p>Each form indicates its required fields. Leaving a required field blank may prevent GFI-CO SARL from handling the request. Optional fields can be left blank where the form allows. The fields actually used and their required status must remain consistent with this policy.</p>

    <h2>7. Recipients</h2>
    <p>Data may be accessed by authorised GFI-CO SARL staff handling enquiries, technical providers needed for website hosting, maintenance or security, and competent authorities where the law provides for this. Data is not intended for sale. <strong>To verify:</strong> the recipients and providers actually used, including the request transmission route and technical providers.</p>

    <h2>8. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>OpenStreetMap may supply map resources loaded by the website. WhatsApp is an external service used at the visitor’s choice. These providers have their own rules and policies. See <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>, the <a href="https://osmfoundation.org/">OpenStreetMap Foundation</a> and <a href="https://www.whatsapp.com/legal/privacy-policy">WhatsApp’s Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>9. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>The actual use of cookies or similar technologies, any audience measurement tools and the preference management options must be checked on the deployed website. Trackers that require consent should only be activated after valid consent has been obtained and appropriate information provided.</p>

    <h2>10. Retention period</h2>
    <p>Data should be retained for a period proportionate to its purpose and applicable obligations. GFI-CO must determine actual periods for unanswered contact requests, quotation requests, client files and technical logs. At the end of the relevant period, data should be deleted or anonymised unless continued retention is necessary or legally required.</p>

    <h2>11. Security</h2>
    <p>GFI-CO SARL implements proportionate technical and organisational measures to protect data against loss, alteration, disclosure or unauthorised access. These may include limiting access, protecting administrator accounts, updating components and making backups where necessary.</p>

    <h2>12. Individual rights</h2>
    <p>Subject to applicable law, you may request information about processing, access your data, ask for inaccurate or incomplete data to be corrected, request deletion, or object to certain processing. Exceptions may apply, including where retention is legally required.</p>

    <h2>13. How to exercise your rights</h2>
    <p>For questions or requests about your data, contact GFI-CO SARL at <a href="mailto:contact@gfi-co.net">contact@gfi-co.net</a>, or by post at [full official address to be completed], with the subject “Personal data request”. GFI-CO may ask for information needed to verify your identity where this is necessary and proportionate. You may also contact the <a href="https://www.autoritedeprotection.ci/">Ivorian authority responsible for personal data protection</a>.</p>

    <h2>14. Data transfers</h2>
    <p>The hosting location, service providers and any transfers of data outside Côte d’Ivoire must be verified. Any transfer must be identified and handled in accordance with applicable requirements.</p>

    <h2>15. Children</h2>
    <p>The website is not specifically intended for children. If processing concerns a child’s personal data, GFI-CO SARL applies the protections and safeguards required by applicable law.</p>

    <h2>16. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>This policy may be updated to reflect changes to the website, data practices or applicable rules. The update date appears at the top of the page. People concerned will be informed of substantial changes where required.</p>

    <h2>17. Contact</h2>
    <p>For questions about this policy or the processing of your data, contact GFI-CO SARL at <a href="mailto:contact@gfi-co.net">contact@gfi-co.net</a>, by telephone at [official number to be confirmed], or at [full official address to be completed].</p>
{% endblock %}
